<div class="tray-title-small">
<span>Character Sheet</span>
<div class="control-mode-toggles">
    {{#if canCleanup}}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-broom control-cleanup" title="{{cleanupTooltip}}"></i>
    {{#if canUseCompendiums}}<span class="control-toggle-separator"></span>{{/if}}
    {{/if}}
    {{#if canUseCompendiums}}
    <i class="fa-solid fa-user control-mode-toggle" data-mode="sheet" title="Show This Character's Items"></i>
    <i class="fa-solid fa-magnifying-glass control-mode-toggle" data-mode="search" title="{{compendiumToggleTitle}}"></i>
    {{/if}}
</div>
</div>
{{!--
    The filter bar. Fourteen chips in three groups, all obeying one rule:

        Every chip names a bucket. A row hides when its bucket is off. A row in
        no bucket in a group is untouched by that group.

    The groups differ only in how completely they cover the rows, and that falls
    out of the data rather than out of behaviour anyone has to learn. Every row
    has exactly one item type, so turning off all five empties the tray. Every
    row has at least one action cost — Passive is what guarantees it — so the
    same is true there. Only some rows can answer "equipped?" or "prepared?", so
    turning off all four of those leaves the rows that answer neither.

    That last case is why the availability group is four chips rather than two
    toggles: a toggle can only hide one side, which made "what am I carrying but
    not wearing" impossible to ask.
--}}
<div class="control-filter-bar">
<div class="filter-group">
<i class="fa-solid fa-heart filter-chip" data-filter-kind="type" data-filter-value="favorites" data-tooltip="Favorites section"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-swords filter-chip" data-filter-kind="type" data-filter-value="weapons" data-tooltip="Weapons — hides them everywhere, favorites included"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-sparkles filter-chip" data-filter-kind="type" data-filter-value="spells" data-tooltip="Spells — hides them everywhere, favorites included"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-stars filter-chip" data-filter-kind="type" data-filter-value="features" data-tooltip="Features — hides them everywhere, favorites included"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-backpack filter-chip" data-filter-kind="type" data-filter-value="inventory" data-tooltip="Inventory — hides it everywhere, favorites included"></i>
</div>
<span class="filter-separator"></span>
<div class="filter-group">
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-a filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="action" data-tooltip="Costs an action"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-b filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="bonus" data-tooltip="Costs a bonus action"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-r filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="reaction" data-tooltip="Costs a reaction"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-s filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="special" data-tooltip="Special activation"></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-square-p filter-chip" data-filter-kind="action" data-filter-value="passive" data-tooltip="Costs no turn action — gear, passives, and anything slower than a turn"></i>
</div>
<span class="filter-separator"></span>
<div class="filter-group">
<i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved filter-chip" data-filter-kind="state" data-filter-value="equipped" data-tooltip="Equipped gear. Says nothing about spells or features."></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-shield-slash filter-chip" data-filter-kind="state" data-filter-value="unequipped" data-tooltip="Gear you are carrying but not wearing or wielding."></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-sun filter-chip" data-filter-kind="state" data-filter-value="prepared" data-tooltip="Prepared spells, plus cantrips and anything always available."></i>
<i class="fa-solid fa-moon filter-chip" data-filter-kind="state" data-filter-value="unprepared" data-tooltip="Spells you know but have not prepared."></i>
</div>
</div>
<div class="control-search">
<input type="text" class="global-search" placeholder="Search All Sections...">
<i class="fa-solid fa-times search-clear" title="Clear Search"></i>
</div>
{{#if canAddFromCompendiums}}
<label class="control-search-option" title="On: adding empties the search box and stays here, for adding several things. Off: adding returns to the character sheet and scrolls to the new item.">
<input type="checkbox" class="compendium-clear-on-add" {{#if clearOnAdd}}checked{{/if}}>
<span>Clear search and keep open on add</span>
</label>
{{/if}}
